{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"approximate","name":"Libye","category":"historical-name","source":"Herodotus, Histories, book IV; Natural Earth 1:50m Cultural Vectors, Admin 0 Countries, version 5.1.2, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/v5.1.2/geojson/ne_50m_admin_0_countries.geojson, SHA-256 3e458fc036ad0a66411f2c1e6cac49c5d7bfb81cb1123bc513b22511a2b7fdeb; Natural Earth 1:10m Physical Vectors, Rivers + lake centerlines, version 5.1.2, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/v5.1.2/geojson/ne_10m_rivers_lake_centerlines.geojson, SHA-256 bb854a900ecbd3b408df46d5e16e3e0f974ba55993f9d8b5c26e855273c0905a","citation":"Herodotus, Histories IV.41–42 (trans. G. C. Macaulay, 1890): « after Egypt Libya succeeds at once » and « Libya furnishes proofs about itself that it is surrounded by sea, except so much of it as borders upon Asia »; IV.181: the Ammonians (Siwa), ten days' journey from Thebes, live in Libya; IV.197: Libyans live in the north of Libya and Ethiopians in the south.","derivation":"Built by social/video/areas.mjs: Africa's land minus the part of Egypt (Natural Earth Admin 0, ADM0_A3 EGY) east of the Nile, so that Libya begins after Egypt's Nile and keeps Siwa; only the mainland is kept (islands such as Madagascar are dropped); Africa's land is the union of the Natural Earth Admin 0 countries whose CONTINENT is Africa; « west of the Nile » keeps, on each grid row, the cells west of the westernmost crossing of the Natural Earth rivers named Nile, El Bahr el Abyad or Bahr el Jebel; north of the river's last vertex (the delta apex near Cairo) the apex longitude is used; on a 0.05° grid (cells whose centre falls inside), traced back as the cell boundary, simplified by Douglas–Peucker at 0.05° and rounded to 0.01°; parts and holes under 5000 km² dropped. Herodotus drew no map: his Libya is the whole continent after Egypt, and he knew its south only from the report of a voyage around it. The valley's west bank, which he counted as Egypt (II.18), is under one pixel at this scale.","licence":"Geometry: Public domain (Natural Earth terms of use: « All versions of Natural Earth raster + vector map data found on this website are in the public domain »). Credit: Made with Natural Earth. Text: Macaulay's translation (1890) is in the public domain.","date":"c. 430 BCE"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[9.68,37.35],[9.13,37.2],[8.73,36.95],[7.98,36.85],[7.83,36.85],[7.53,37.05],[7.28,37.1],[7.2,37.08],[7.23,36.95],[6.98,36.9],[6.58,37],[6.48,37.1],[6.08,36.85],[5.68,36.8],[5.38,36.65],[5.23,36.65],[4.83,36.9],[3.73,36.9],[3.58,36.8],[2.98,36.8],[2.63,36.6],[1.38,36.55],[0.38,36.2],[0.18,36.1],[-0.02,35.85],[-0.17,35.8],[-0.47,35.85],[-0.87,35.7],[-1.87,35.1],[-2.68,35.1],[-2.85,35.17],[-2.97,35.4],[-3.32,35.2],[-4.02,35.25],[-4.27,35.15],[-4.67,35.2],[-5.02,35.4],[-5.3,35.67],[-5.32,35.9],[-5.92,35.8],[-6.4,34.67],[-6.92,33.95],[-7.62,33.6],[-8.37,33.35],[-9.25,32.58],[-9.3,32.17],[-9.7,31.67],[-9.85,31.17],[-9.85,30.67],[-9.65,30.48],[-9.65,30.13],[-10.15,29.42],[-10.62,28.95],[-11.12,28.7],[-11.47,28.35],[-12.02,28.1],[-12.87,27.95],[-13.2,27.63],[-13.5,26.83],[-13.82,26.55],[-14.45,26.23],[-14.5,25.92],[-14.8,25.42],[-14.85,24.83],[-15,24.58],[-15.17,24.5],[-15.9,23.83],[-15.8,23.73],[-16.2,23.13],[-16.15,23.03],[-16.35,22.73],[-16.35,22.58],[-16.57,22.3],[-16.8,22.18],[-16.95,21.88],[-17.1,20.98],[-17.07,20.85],[-17,21.03],[-16.87,21.1],[-16.7,20.73],[-16.57,20.6],[-16.52,20.7],[-16.4,20.63],[-16.2,20.22],[-16.25,19.83],[-16.4,19.58],[-16.35,19.42],[-16.5,19.33],[-16.25,19.08],[-16.15,18.83],[-16.05,18.42],[-16.05,17.58],[-16.45,16.67],[-16.55,16.27],[-16.55,15.77],[-16.65,15.58],[-17.15,14.92],[-17.5,14.72],[-17.23,14.7],[-16.95,14.38],[-16.8,14.02],[-16.65,14.02],[-16.75,13.88],[-16.42,13.35],[-16.17,13.45],[-15.8,13.42],[-16.12,13.4],[-16.42,13.25],[-16.62,13.45],[-16.8,13.38],[-16.75,13.13],[-16.8,12.67],[-16.73,12.6],[-16.62,12.7],[-16.45,12.63],[-16.73,12.55